pySMESH: NETGEN_Remesher_2D runs with no NETGEN_RemesherParameters_2D (NETGENPlugin
V9_16_0; applies after NETGENPlugin_remesher_stl_topology.patch).

Defect: NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D::Compute calls
ngMesh->LoadLocalMeshSize( ngParams.meshsize_filename ). With a parameters hypothesis the
name is that hypothesis's mesh size file, "" by default. Without one it is the null pointer
that the Ng_Meshing_Parameters constructor sets (nglib.cpp), and the std::string that
Mesh::LoadLocalMeshSize takes is built from it: an access violation (0xC0000005) in every
remesh with no parameters (pySMESH record g3/nr1_min.py, "without").

Change, in NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx only: LoadLocalMeshSize is called only for a name.
Nothing else changes.

diff --git a/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx b/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx
--- a/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx
+++ b/src/NETGENPlugin/NETGENPlugin_Remesher_2D.cxx
@@ -723,7 +723,10 @@
   ngMesh->SetLocalH( stlTopo->GetBoundingBox().PMin() - netgen::Vec3d(h, h, h),
                      stlTopo->GetBoundingBox().PMax() + netgen::Vec3d(h, h, h),
                      netgen::mparam.grading );
-  ngMesh->LoadLocalMeshSize( ngParams.meshsize_filename );
+  // pySMESH: with no NETGEN_RemesherParameters_2D the file name is the null pointer of
+  // a default Ng_Meshing_Parameters, and a std::string made from it read address 0.
+  if ( ngParams.meshsize_filename )
+    ngMesh->LoadLocalMeshSize( ngParams.meshsize_filename );
 
   netgen::OCCGeometry occgeo;
   mesher.SetLocalSize( occgeo, *ngMesh );
